  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1210 AM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nFor much of the upcoming week, the broad subtropical ridge axis \nremains the dominant weather feature across much of the southern \nU.S. There are some differences noted in the operational runs of the \nGFS and ECMWF in showing some potential for weakening of the ridge \nlate in the forecast period. While the GFS solution favors an upper \ntrough developing over the southern U.S. plains late in the period, \nensembles from both of the mentioned models do not agree. For now, \nwe prefer to keep the forecast dry along with temperatures remaining \nabove climatological normals for mid to late August.",
